  "method": "Paired measurement application: same 100 rows, 64-byte BLOB payload, STRICT/FK schema and named AOT queries; plain omits secondary/partial unique indexes and all triggers, indexed-trigger includes feed/expression indexes and audit/counter triggers. Both retain the PK index. Browser main-thread AotDatabase plus real strict IndexedDB; no Worker RPC or server sync. Three fresh browser cold loads per profile; actual Brotli HTTP body bytes include HTML, runtime/IDB adapter and Program JSON. First sample separately times 7x200 point reads and 7x50 durable title updates after warmup. Audit rows grow on updates only with triggers; their costs are part of that workload. Separate 64-update sampled peak (no forced GC); retained/after are forced-GC heap, backing storage separate, not exact transient peak or RSS. Native typed output and replay checked in each sample. Timing is ms/operation.",
